# Avoid direct global access

`window`, `document`, `navigator`, `localStorage`, `process.env`, and `globalThis` are the runtime. Reading them in application code hides a dependency. Unit tests then need jsdom or a stubbed environment. This is a Node.js bot. Application code has no browser.

Inject env, clock, timers, and `fetch` at the composition root. Pass values inward. Tests and `src/main.ts` / `src/composition/` may touch the real runtime. Do not call `Date.now()`, `new Date()` without arguments, `setTimeout`, `setInterval`, or global `fetch` in application logic. See time-is-an-external-dependency.mdc and [ADR-013](../../docs/adr/013-inject-fetch-no-try-catch.md).

```typescript
type Environment = { readonly apiKey: string };

// ❌ Hidden runtime. Mocha would need jsdom or a fake process.env.
function readApiKey(): string {
    return process.env.API_KEY ?? '';
}

// ✅ The entry file reads the environment once and passes data in.
function createBrokerClient(environment: Environment) {
    return { apiKey: environment.apiKey };
}
```
